=== Acceptance summary ===
[x] Surface renders every web-source state: photo present/absent; live-state hero (4 RadialGauges + 8-cell StatCard grid);
    and the no-live-state OFFLINE card (identity + StatusBadge(offline) + a friendly EmptyState in the metrics region +
    actions) — never a blank box. Fetch-driven loading/error/stale/offline are N/A for a pure presentational surface
    (web VehicleHeroCard has no data feed); modelling them would fabricate behaviour (Honesty Covenant #2/#9), matching
    the accepted sibling MetricCard/StickyChipBar precedent. Documented in the model + view headers.
[x] Hooks bind via shared P1/S8 state holders: useUnits -> LocalDataContainer.unitFormatter (StateFlow<UnitFormatter>);
    useTranslation -> P1/S10 catalog (stringResource). vehicle/vehicleState/photoUrl are caller props (web parity). No HTTP in the view.
[x] i18n: all 19 source keys already exist in strings.xml (translation_vehicleHero_*, translation_common_on/off/offline);
    no English literals in native code; no catalog change needed.
[x] Accessibility: each RadialGauge exposes a "label: value" content description; StatCards expose label+value; the three
    action Buttons carry their localized labels as accessible names; the photo frame carries the localized alt ("<name> photo").
[x] SI->display at the render boundary only (convertDistanceFromSI/convertTempFromSI); power rendered via fmtNumber parity
    (Tesla drive_state.power is kW on the wire, not divided from watts) — Phase-48 SI-canonical respected.
[x] Tests: ModelTest (projection adapter + conversions + thresholds + status + diagnostics, 12 cases, all green) +
    UiTest (per-state render + a11y labels, mirrors the accepted MetricCardUiTest harness).
[x] No TODO/stub/mock/placeholder/Lorem in shipped code (check-placeholders PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0).
[x] Telemetry: one-shot view.opened with slug "VehicleHeroCard" (PII-safe; no name/VIN/battery/range), P1/S11.

